  "query_preview": "..\nThe fog is slowly dissipating across the area in river basins. A\nlight west wind tonight will most likely keep the fog at bay.\n\nLook for seasonable weather to continue before an upper trough \napproaches the region to finish out the week along with a surface \ncold front. Ensembles continue to keep much of the QPF southwest \nof the CWA. Thus, will maintain a dry forecast for now.\n\nOver the weekend, upper ridging looks to rebound with dry weather\nconditions and warming temperatures. Highs across NE Montana for\nSunday will reach into the 50s and 60s. This will be short lived\nhowever, as the next cold front will bring in breezy conditions\nSunday night and cooler temperatures for Monday.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\nNBM held the line for this forecast cycle with mostly dry weather\nconditions and little in the way of major temperature swings, save\nfor warmer temperatures on Sunday. Therefore, little in the way in\ndeviation was needed.",
